.TH LBM_PRO 1 "October 2026" "wind-tunnel-2d" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbm_pro \- validated 2D lattice-Boltzmann solver with interactive window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbm_pro
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbm_pro
fuses the validated solver core from
.BR lbm_bench (1)
(TRT collision, Bouzidi curved walls, Guo 2nd-order in/outflow,
q-consistent Mei-Luo-Shyy momentum exchange) into the interactive SDL
shell of
.BR lbm_tunnel (1).
It is
.BR "cylinder-only faithful" :
it runs exactly one configuration, straight duct with a circular cylinder,
because that is the only setup the Bouzidi curved wall is validated for.
The
.B G
(geometry cycle) and
.B O
(obstacle cycle) keys from
.BR lbm_tunnel (1)
are deliberately absent, and
.BR LB_GEOM / LB_OBS
environment overrides are ignored.
.PP
Live Cd and Cl (q-consistent momentum exchange, EMA-smoothed) appear on
the HUD once the EMA warms up (~2000 steps). An optional Smagorinsky LES
closure extends the stable range past the laminar ceiling at the cost of
not being benchmark-validated.
.SH CONTROLS
Keyboard controls track
.BR lbm_tunnel (1)
where they map, except:
.TP
.B "G, O, C"
Removed. The configuration is fixed.
.TP
.B +\~/\~\(mi\~/\~0
Grow/shrink/reset the
.I cylinder
size (still a circle, still gets Bouzidi, still faithful).
.TP
.B K
Toggle Smagorinsky LES (Cs = 0.17). Needed only above about Re = 250
where the laminar scheme fails. The HUD annotates
.B +LES (unvalidated).
.TP
.B P
Transient symmetry-breaking seed (as in
.BR lbm_tunnel (1)).
.TP
.B F
Speed/vorticity colouring.
.TP
.B V
MP4 recording (writes
.BR lbm_pro_<timestamp>.mp4 ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LB_SELFTEST=1
Run headless. Reports mean velocity, mass conservation, Cd (mean), Cl
(mean/amplitude/rms), St (from Cl zero-crossings), and solver status.
.TP
.B "LB_STEPS LB_MACH LB_TAU LB_PERTURB"
Overrides.
.BR LB_GEOM / LB_OBS
are deliberately
.B not
honoured.
.TP
.B LB_SMAG
Smagorinsky Cs. 0 disables (default); 0.14-0.18 are typical if enabling.
.TP
.B LB_CSV=path
Write per-step time series (step, probe uy, Cd, Cl) to
.IR path .
Analysable via
.BR tools/analyze.py .
.TP
.B LB_CP=path
Write azimuthal
.IR "C_p(theta)"
around the cylinder (theta = 0 at upstream stagnation) to
.IR path .
Textbook comparison with Henderson-Williamson curves.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Watch, with symmetry-breaking seed to trigger shedding:
.PP
.RS
.B ./lbm_pro
.RE
.PP
(then press P to seed the wake)
.PP
Headless, dump time series and
.IR C_p :
.PP
.RS
.B LB_SELFTEST=1 LB_STEPS=4000 LB_MACH=0.10 LB_PERTURB=1 \\
.br
.B LB_CSV=ts.csv LB_CP=cp.csv ./lbm_pro
.br
.B python3 tools/analyze.py both ts.csv cp.csv
.RE
.PP
LES-on stress test above the laminar BGK ceiling:
.PP
.RS
.B LB_SELFTEST=1 LB_MACH=0.40 LB_PERTURB=1 LB_SMAG=0.17 LB_STEPS=3000 \\
.br
.B ./lbm_pro
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B lbm_pro_<ISO-timestamp>.mp4
Written when
.B V
is pressed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wind_tunnel (1),
.BR lbm_tunnel (1),
.BR lbm_bench (1)
.SH NOTES
"Validated" transfers to
.B lbm_pro
because the cylinder path is the same code
.BR lbm_bench (1)
reproduced Schaefer-Turek 2D-2 with. The LES closure, when enabled, is
standard but not benchmark-validated.
